   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The twelve animals",
     "texto": [
      "In Vietnam the solar calendar (**dương lịch**) is used for daily life and the lunar (**âm lịch**) for traditional festivals. The lunar zodiac cycle assigns an animal to each year and repeats every 12 years.",
      "It's very common to be asked: **Anh tuổi con gì?** = What animal are you? Answer: **Tôi tuổi con rồng.** = I'm a dragon.",
      "In the Vietnamese zodiac, the fourth animal is the **cat (mèo)**; in other zodiacs in the region the rabbit may appear.",
      "The traditional Sino-Vietnamese names (Tý, Sửu, Dần…) appear in calendars and expressions: **Tôi tuổi Thìn** = I was born in the year of the dragon.",
      "The lunar new year is the **Tết Nguyên Đán** (or simply Tết). It used to be celebrated with firecrackers (**pháo**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
